1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:04,416
For the longest time, automation meant writing scripts — if this, then that.

2
00:00:04,366 --> 00:00:07,325
You had to anticipate every branch, every edge case.

3
00:00:07,325 --> 00:00:09,516
But LLM-based agents are different.

4
00:00:09,516 --> 00:00:11,208
They don't follow rules.

5
00:00:11,208 --> 00:00:13,925
They reason through situations they've never seen before.

6
00:00:13,925 --> 00:00:19,025
They read your codebase, pull from multiple sources, string together a plan, and write working output.

7
00:00:19,025 --> 00:00:22,158
The key thing to understand is: this is not a tool upgrade.

8
00:00:22,158 --> 00:00:24,058
It's a new category of worker.

